  'outs gained' is |r| x residual sd: the sd of the part of the
  residual this feature could remove. Against ~2.7 outs of real
  between-start variation, anything under ~0.2 is not worth
  building. 'opp K% (model)' and 'predicted outs' are CONTROLS:
  they already feed the simulation, so a large value there means
  the model is mis-USING what it already has.
